00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:34,440
What am I to do?

281
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,200
What was me?

282
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,080
I'll just act randomly.

283
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,600
But that would not be what a sensible person would

284
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,200
do based with this.

285
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,360
The sensible thing is just to go and plug the numbers

286
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:47,640
into expected utility theory and do that.

287
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,280
That's a sensible thing.

288
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,040
So anyway, so just because you're ignorant

289
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:53,760
doesn't mean that you are stupid.

290
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:56,520
So if you don't know exactly what's going on,

291
00:12:56,520 --> 00:13:00,640
you could just fall back on more general purpose strategies.

292
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,720
Fall back on more general purpose strategies

293
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,600
to take account of all the possible outcomes.

294
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,120
Say, well, let's see.

295
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,560
So this job seems more fun, but it's higher risk.

296
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:12,720
So let me weigh the pros and cons.

297
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:15,280
And again, if there's someone that actually

298
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:18,360
knows better than you, then of course there is, well,

299
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:20,600
how about just listen to them?

300
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,480
But on the other hand, if nobody knows any better than you do,

301
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:27,200
then whatever your best guess is is, as far as anyone knows,

302
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,920
the best guess about what anyone should do.

303
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:31,840
What you should do.

304
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:35,280
And that is the solution.

305
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:40,320
So we say, well, look, mountain climbing.

306
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,880
Mountain climbing is a market failure

307
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,420
because people don't know if they're

308
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:45,280
going to make it to the top.

309
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:51,160
Well, as long as they've got probabilities right,

310
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,440
who knows better about the probabilities of mountain

311
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,040
climbers?

312
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:56,520
If anyone of them, they would seem like they know the best.

313
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:58,360
And they know their own limitations

314
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,720
better than anyone else.

315
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:02,760
So why wouldn't they just go and optimize his bank utility,

316
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:06,440
taking into account all the possibilities of top,

317
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:10,240
or fail, or get a little frostbite, or lose fingers,

318
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:13,680
or follow your death, or PTSD, all

319
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,480
these different possibilities.

320
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,280
So if you've seen mountain climbing movies,

321
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:20,840
you know about all the horrible things that happen to them.

322
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:24,920
Just rewatch this great one about 1936

323
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:28,640
ascent of the north face of the Eiger in Switzerland,

324
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:33,200
where they all died, just to give it away.

